SM(368,{"n":"Numbers 20","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/Numbers 20.mp3","d":2636.7,"s":[[0.32,"Come and study the Holy Scriptures with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Counsel of God."],[9.04,"Father Stephen holds a PhD in Biblical Studies, and is an Orthodox priest serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[23.52,"Okay. We'll go ahead and get started."],[25.52,"We're going to get started here."],[27.04,"In just a moment, we're going to be picking up at the beginning of Numbers chapter 20."],[32.88,"And so we left off last time at another place where sort of the genre of the text shifted again."],[40.88,"As we've talked about now many times."],[43.92,"Book of Numbers covers about 40 years of the history of Israel in the wilderness."],[50.88,"And so we get all kinds of stuff."],[54.1,"All brought together here."],[56.18,"We get narrative episodes."],[58.5,"We get uh commandments, we get liturgical instructions, we get a census at the beginning and another one at the end."],[67.44,"We get all kinds of material in here."],[69.36,"And so and when it shifts, it can shift kind of abruptly."],[74.72,"Now, as we saw last time, we had an episode talking about who held the priesthood, and then we had commandments for priests."],[82.25,"So it's not that it's just totally arbitrary and jumbled and thrown together."],[85.71,"There is a rhyme and a reason to it as to where these things are inserted and how it's been brought together, but it is the bringing together of a whole bunch of different material."],[94.91,"And we're about to start another narrative section."],[97.55,"Last time we were talking about those commandments aimed to a priests."],[101.31,"As we've talked about the narrative sections, we're not giv.en all like super detail on the 40 years"],[107.91,"So as we talked about between uh Mount Sinai in the middle of Exodus and a few chapters into the Book of Numbers was two years."],[119.35,"Between that point in the Book of Numbers and the end of the Book of Numbers is 40 years."],[124.81,"So that gives you an idea of the difference in level of detail in terms of the no of uh how comprehensive our narrative is."],[134.99,"Of events. So we're just sort of spot checking in."],[138.19,"We don't always get an amount of time that's passed, but we spot check in on these sort of major events that take place during that 40 years high."],[147.75,"Hop from one to the other, and then based on the themes that are understood as being related to those events, we'll have some other material related to that theme brought in before the next event."],[159.61,"That's sort of in general the kind of structure that we're dealing with."],[164.89,"So now we're gonna be shifting."],[166.46,"And we're gonna see really the beginning of this chapter, beginning tonight, we are shifting sort of into the end game."],[177.18,"We aren't given an exact again, amount of time passed, in terms of how close this is to them arriving at Canaan at the end of the 40 years."],[188.0,"But as we're gonna see right off the bat, uh and, over the the course of tonight, we're drawing we're we're now much closer to the end of that than beginning."],[198.78,"It only began a few chapters ago, but now we're we're on the other side of that."],[203.82,"Okay. And so we're going to shift into some of the events that we're gonna be reading about, some of the some of the other material is now gonna be shifting towards, okay, now that older generation that came out of Egypt is dying off, new next generation is coming of age, and them making preparations then to go into Canaan."],[231.58,"So that shift really, that pivot point is really where we're at tonight."],[235.9,"And we'll see that right off the bat"],[235.92,"We've left the build up."],[238.08,"Now we're shifting into that mode."],[242.64,"So unless anybody has any leftover comments or questions or anarcho primitivist lifestyles that don't involve starving to death, uh, we will go pick go ahead and pick up in Numbers chapter 20, verse 1."],[257.92,"Now the children of Israel, the whole congregation, came into the desert of sin in the first month, and the people stayed in Kadesh, and Miriam died and was buried there."],[267.92,"So this is what I meant by right off the bat."],[270.96,"Okay, so we've had sort of the three people who are at the top of sort of the hierarchy in the camp are, of course, Moses M.oses, as the leader, Aaron the high priest and' sister Miriam"],[285.74,"Okay, so now Miriam has passed away."],[289.58,"So we're seeing the beginning of the end of that generation."],[294.46,"Remember, Miriam is the one who led the song after they crossed the Red Sea."],[298.59,"And so now she has passed away, she has been buried there."],[303.87,"Don't read a ton into the desert of sin because the English word sin is not related."],[312.35,"Yeah, it is related to Sinai."],[315.87,"The Sinai Desert is in like the Sinai Peninsula, which is where they've been wandering."],[321.71,"What about Kaddish?"],[323.07,"Because I had a vague idea that ancient Kadesh was north of Israel."],[324.91,"No No, Kadesh is Kaddish was, depending on what point in history we're talking about."],[340.68,"Was at the far eastern edge of Egyptian territory and power."],[347.16,"So the not very good."],[350.28,"Yes. The not the not very good movie uh with Christian Bale playing Moses."],[355.66,"Exodus Gods and Kings, I think it was called."],[359.26,"No, no. Christian Bale."],[360.46,"It was Christian Baile is Moses."],[362.14,"Uh not a very good movie, but based on where they place the timeline, the first 20 minutes of it are an incredibly good historical recreation of the Battle of Kaddish."],[369.02,"Where the Egyptians fought the Hittites"],[376.32,"So the Hittites had come down right across the Levant and were at the edge of sort of Egyptian, at the edge of the."],[385.76,"So we're where the Sinai Peninsula meets the Levant, is the idea."],[389.52,"And so, yes, I recommend the first 20 minutes of that movie and then turning it off."],[394.4,"Because it just gets weird."],[396.4,"So there are two things there."],[398.0,"Number one, Miriam."],[399.44,"Number two, they're now moving back closer to Canaan."],[405.28,"Now, they're not going to immediately go up into Canaan."],[411.44,"God said why back at Exodus, because if they went up the coast, they'd have to go through Philistine territory."],[413.28,"Because that's where the Philistine cities are"],[420.76,"Philistine territory was centered around five major cities."],[426.44,"The biblical ones you one main biblical one you've heard of is Got or Gath, where Goliath was from."],[433.32,"But also Ashkelon, Ashdod, they're all along the coast."],[437.72,"Where the Philistines settled after they and the rest of the sea peoples tried to invade Egypt and failed."],[442.68,"So they settled along the coast."],[445.0,"And God said earlier that uh when they first left Egypt, that they weren't going to go through that territory because he knew that the Israelites would chicken out."],[456.44,"They ended up chickening out anyway. but he knew they would chicken out if he tried to go through Philistine territory because they were too militarily powerful and they'd get scared"],[465.28,"We're gonna read something else about the Philistines in Deuteronomy, but that's a teaser uh for when we get to the beginning of Deuteronomy in a couple of months."],[474.0,"We'll find out some more about the Philistines and who they're descended from."],[478.72,"But so they're moving back into that area."],[481.12,"They're gonna end up looping around."],[482.64,"We'll see that here in just a few verses."],[484.72,"The the sort of path they take."],[486.8,"Um, but so they've drawn back into proximity, and Miriam, who's obviously a major figure in that initial generation that came out of Egypt, has passed away."],[497.2,"Verse 2, but there was no water for the congregation."],[500.72,"So they gathered together against Moses and Aaron."],[503.32,"So the people scoffed at Moses and spoke, saying, Would we had died in the destruction of our brethren before the Lord?"],[510.2,"Why have you brought up the Lord's congregation into this desert to kill us and our cattle?"],[517.24,"Who does who does who does this sound like?"],[520.2,"They're sounding a lot like their parents."],[522.28,"Yeah. That generation."],[525.7,"Why did you bring us here to die, Moses?"],[529.35,"There's no water."],[530.87,"And so we've talked about this before, I know, but the and our cattle."],[535.45,"This is this is a sort of Hebrew way of speaking."],[540.51,"To kind of take something to an extreme."],[542.91,"The idea being, don't you uh at least care about the cows."],[546.85,"If you don't care about us, why don't you care that you're gonna be mean to the cows?"],[550.05,"What did the cow do you"],[551.42,"You get one of the most famous places you see this is the end of the book of Jonah."],[555.43,"Where God says to Jonah, like, you're all upset that this tree died there for a couple of days."],[562.44,"And you know, in this city, there's all these thousands of people, and a lot of cats, and all these cattle."],[568.98,"Don't you at least care about the cows?"],[571.62,"Why did you also bring us up out of Egypt to bring us to this evil place?"],[575.78,"A place where nothing is sown, neither figs nor vines, nor pomegranates, nor is there any water to drink."],[581.86,"So we're back to this again."],[584.56,"This shows us something important, though."],[586.82,"Remember that that. previous generation died in the wilderness"],[590.46,"Why are we now seeing the next generation doing the same thing?"],[594.06,"It's not that the next generation were just all, no, we're all, you know, we're not like our parents."],[599.34,"We're all obedient and wonderful and love God and keep all the commandments."],[603.98,"And no, they're just as bad."],[606.55,"And God's going to emphasize this in Deuteronomy."],[609.53,"Like, you didn't earn this."],[611.05,"You're not like better."],[613.39,"You're marginally better than the actual Canaanites who you're gonna be displacing."],[617.65,"Who are committing real abominations."],[619.65,"But you're not righteous and wonderful, and you're right."],[623.65,"That's why uh we're doing this."],[626.05,"So Moses and Aaron went from the presence of the congregation to the door of the tabernacle of testimony and fell on their faces."],[631.25,"Then the glory of the Lord appeared to them"],[637.61,"So here we go again."],[639.87,"So they go to God."],[641.71,"What do we do?"],[642.91,"The Lord then spoke to Moses, saying, Take the rod, and you and your brother Aaron, gather the congregation together, speak to the rock before them, and it will give its waters."],[653.63,"Thus you shall bring them water out of the rock and give drink to the congregation and their cattle."],[659.71,"So this should be giving you a little bit of deja vu."],[662.83,"I know it's been a long time, probably like a year."],[666.03,"But not only did this is this grumbling sort of deja vu, but there was a whole water issue."],[674.35,"Back when they first came out of Egypt into the wilderness."],[675.79,"We don't have any water"],[678.15,"Why'd you bring us out here to die?"],[680.24,"And you remember at that time, God said to Moses, I'm going to go stand on the rock."],[689.68,"And you're to go out there and strike the rock with the rod, and it will bring forth water."],[699.2,"And we talked about, we we talked about at the time a couple of things."],[704.0,"One of those was so what did that symbolize."],[706.82,"Well, the rod is representative, as we've seen all through this in the Torah, the rod represents judgment."],[714.36,"If you're a shepherd, the rod is what you use for discipline."],[716.72,"I mean, you need to whack a sheep back into the poking stick."],[722.61,"And so, remember, he went when they turned the Nile into blood, he went and struck the water with the rod."],[729.91,"So this is like pronouncing judgment."],[733.27,"So in that first case, there's this dispute between the Israelites and God."],[740.71,"And the Israelites are accusing God, basically."],[744.71,"They're accusing God."],[745.75,"You brought us out here to die."],[747.84,"They're imputing God's motives."],[749.52,"They're making this accusation against him."],[752.08,"And we talked about how God saying, Well, I'll stand on the rock, and you strike the rock, and it'll give bring forth water."],[760.32,"Was a demonstration of the humility of God, which is a strange phrase."],[762.72,"God. The idea that is humble"],[768.13,"Like, how what?"],[770.31,"Like, but we talked about."],[774.23,"One of the unique things about the God of Israel is that he has humility, even though it seems like a contradiction."],[780.95,"He's the God of the Israelites."],[783.27,"This made no sense to Pharaoh."],[785.51,"The God of a bunch of slaves is trying to tell me what to do."],[788.39,"Well, he can't be a very good God because his people are slaves."],[792.36,"Like, you know?"],[793.68,"like Like, you're a bunch of losers."],[795.32,"He's like, I'm Pharaoh."],[797.16,"I'm the head of the greatest superpower in the world."],[799.8,"I think my gods are probably better then."],[802.22,"Because I'm way more powerful than you guys are."],[804.78,"God identifies as the god of Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob"],[805.06,"That's how people thought."],[806.26,"But God chooses to identify with them."],[811.7,"Three like nomads who nobody had heard of."],[816.9,"Who didn't even have a country, let alone ruling one, who were just wandering around in tents with their families."],[822.75,"And we've seen as we've gone through the Torah that God identifies himself with orphans and widows and strangers and foreigners and the poor."],[831.57,"Like all the people who are loose, those are the people who God chooses to identify himself with?"],[838.49,"And we talked about how this display of humility at the rock, and that in general, is part of what's pointing us to Jesus as the Messiah."],[852.81,"Messiah refers to a king."],[855.95,"The anointed king, the ruler."],[858.75,"So, what should you, if you understand the Torah."],[863.17,"And what we've been reading, what kind of person would you expect him to be?"],[869.09,"This God's Messiah to be?"],[871.33,"Would you expect him to be like a warrior?"],[875.94,"To be Herod's son, to be the Roman Emperor's son."],[881.11,"No. You'd expect him to be maybe the son of peasants, born under circumstances that got him accused of things, and his mother accused of things."],[892.07,"Born in a cave with a bunch of animals"],[897.19,"Laid in a food trough when he was born."],[900.71,"Dirt poor. Nothing to recommend."],[904.45,"That that's exactly what you should be expecting if you understand that somehow this God, the God, the true God who created the universe, is nonetheless humble and identifies with the humble."],[917.73,"So we talked about that."],[920.21,"We'll come back to that in a second."],[922.37,"We also talked about uh the the the tradition, the Jewish tradition, which is important because St."],[929.01,"Paul refers to it."],[931.97,"It answered the question."],[933.69,"W,ell we read that way back in Exodus, like a year ago."],[935.97,"Now we're reading this in numbers"],[939.85,"They've been wandering in the wilderness for like close to 40 years now, roundabout."],[945.31,"30 some odd."],[947.39,"Where have they been getting the water all this time?"],[952.75,"And so there came to be a tradition that that original rock followed them around."],[961.84,"From place to place."],[963.12,"But they picked up camp and moved."],[965.2,"In fact, if you read uh the Midrash on this, uh, which has a lot of these stories, it has a song that they sang when they wanted the rock to move and catch up to that, and the rock would come and show up where they were."],[981.26,"And say I say St."],[982.54,"Paul refers to this."],[983.42,"Remember, he says in 1 Corinthians, and he just drops this with no explanation."],[989.02,"He just says, Israel had a rock that followed them in the wilderness."],[992.54,"And if all you read was the text of the Torah, you'd be like, followed them."],[997.02,"What? St. Paul just refers to this tradition as being a fact."],[1001.66,"He says the rock was Christ."],[1004.94,"Kind of bearing out what I was just saying a minute ago."],[1007.82,"But that's but so this is important because, for example, St."],[1012.46,"Paul receives the scriptures within a tradition of interpretation."],[1017.02,"And he doesn't distinguish between the two."],[1020.3,"He doesn't say, now listen, Corinthians, you know, it's not in the Bible. but there's this tradition that the rock followed them"],[1031.3,"Doesn't do that."],[1032.5,"Does it remotely do that?"],[1034.02,"He doesn't ever do that."],[1036.6,"When he's talking to Saint Timothy, he talks about Moses contesting with Janus and Jambras."],[1042.44,"And you're like, who?"],[1044.12,"Well, if you know the Jewish tradition, those are the names of Pharaoh's court wizards who contested with Moses."],[1050.12,"Their names ain't in the Torah."],[1052.44,"Again, St. Paul doesn't say, Well, now this isn't in the Bible, but you know, traditionally the names of those wizards were Janus and Jem."],[1062.17,"He just references it because he's received it as part of this whole."],[1067.21,"So there is no sort of bare biblical text or Torah text or something that isn't a part of a tradition of reading it, interpreting it, copying it, handing it down."],[1080.86,"You can't separate those things out."],[1083.5,"I mean, you can verbally, but in reality, you cannot pry those those things apart."],[1088.86,"So, all that said, now this time you see the instructions are a little different."],[1093.42,"He says, Go to the rock."],[1095.26,"Now, let me point out, if you're looking for evidence in the text for that tradition, notice God says the rock."],[1104.94,"Which rock? If this was just another random rock, you'd have to tell them him which one."],[1111.23,"one, It's not like there's only rock in the Sinai Desert?"],[1115.07,"There's a couple."],[1115.95,"Or go find a rock."],[1117.42,"Go to the rock I direct you to."],[1120.6,"Go to this rock."],[1122.26,"That's what I said."],[1123.14,"Go to the rock."],[1124.66,"So apparently Moses immediately knew what rock it was."],[1127.54,"So this could be taken as evidence that that whole following them thing is implied here, even though not stated."],[1134.58,"But he says, go and speak to it."],[1136.66,"And when he speaks to it, God will uh give the Israelites water."],[1150.66,"Verse 9. So Moses took the rod from before the Lord, as the Lord ordered him."],[1153.3,"from before the So this would be took it Lord."],[1158.14,"Remember, this is Aaron's rod, remember it budded, and they put it in the most holy place."],[1163.18,"So they went in there to talk to God."],[1165.58,"Moses goes and takes the rod."],[1167.34,"Then Moses and Aaron gathered the congregation together before the rock."],[1172.3,"And he, Moses, said to them, Hear me, you disobedient ones."],[1176.78,"Must we bring water for you out of this rock?"],[1180.54,"Now this already should send up the danger, Will Robinson."],[1185.92,"Like we? Moses and Aaron, are gonna bring them water out of the rock?"],[1193.52,"Or Moses and God."],[1198.48,"Verse 11 But wait, it gets worse."],[1200.92,"Moses then lifted his hand and struck the rock twice with his rod."],[1206.92,"And water came out abundantly, and the congregation and their cattle drank."],[1211.96,"Well, it's supposed to hit the rock."],[1214.12,"Wasn't supposed to hit the rock twice?"],[1216.6,"Wasn't supposed to present it as oh, here's Moses and Aaron are gonna do a magic trick and give you water."],[1224.44,"What did hitting the rock symbolize the first time?"],[1227.48,"God accepting right the judgment of the people, giving them water and giving them life nonetheless."],[1235.08,"So, what is Moses doing when he strikes the rock?"],[1237.96,"He's judging God in front of the people."],[1243.08,"Because he's angry at them"],[1243.76,"And taking credit for the water they're about to get."],[1250.72,"Oh disobedient ones is a very nice translation."],[1253.94,"Like he's angry at them."],[1256.1,"Possibly a little at God also for the whole situation."],[1259.38,"This again. And so he does this."],[1262.11,"And there are about to be serious consequences."],[1264.35,"Because as we've talked about, you're in a leadership position."],[1269.13,"Like, and Moses is in the highest leadership position possible for humans."],[1273.51,"You are more accountable."],[1276.55,"You are more accountable."],[1278.39,"So, and and this is something you need to know to understand the Old Testament."],[1284.17,"Because this looks like, okay, yeah, he lost his temper and whacked a rock with a stick a couple of times."],[1285.69,"like This seems a fairly minor thing to us by our standards."],[1297.2,"But that's what this accountability is about."],[1300.8,"People, you know, sometimes wonder to me or ask me, they're like, you know, if you're like a monk on Mount Athos, and like you live in a monastery and you're like doing the full cycle of monastic services every day and spending another big chunk of the day in prayer."],[1316.58,"And then working your hands, like what do you talk about when you go to confession?"],[1324.2,"Like, what could you possibly do?"],[1326.36,"Like, how much trouble could you get into, like you know and and that's because we're living in the world and I know what kind of trouble I get into and I'm like well if I I think if I lived there and I had all that to do I wouldn't be doing the things I currently do to get into trouble right but the closer we we get to God the more things that right now would be the least of my issues right like if I was gonna list all my sins they'd be number 378 right on the list when you i i if you actually take care of the first 350 or the first 370, 378 now moves to the top of the list."],[1369.22,"And so what may seem like a little thing to me now, based on how simple I am."],[1374.71,"For someone who's come very close to God, and is who has spent a life in repentance and has achieved a certain level of holiness and is in the presence of God a lot more than I am, those things that seem inconsignificant by comparison are are big things."],[1390.48,"And so Moses, who is as close, I mean, it's talking to God face to face day to day, as close to God as any human being has ever been while they're alive."],[1399.66,"This thing is huge."],[1401.98,"Even though to me, I mean, even among things I've done when I've lost my temper, this would be super low on the list."],[1408.46,"But this is big."],[1410.78,"Because of who Moses is."],[1413.26,"Verse 12. But the Lord spoke to Moses and Aaron, because you did not believe me to sanctify me before the children of Israel, therefore you shall not bring this congregation into the land I am giving them."],[1426.18,"So that's a weird translation."],[1428.34,"You didn't believe me."],[1430.66,"Didn't believe them about what?"],[1435.22,"That doesn't make any sense."],[1437.38,"And then the second piece, to sanctify me before the people of Israel."],[1441.22,"So here's what that actually says."],[1443.56,"So remember, we've talked about the word for believe, and the word for faith is the same word in Greek that this is translated from."],[1449.56,"So the idea here is because you were not faithful to me, because you didn't do what I said."],[1454.28,"You didn't do what I told you to."],[1456.22,"You weren't faithful to do what I told you to do, number one."],[1460.3,"And then number two, sanctify them because you didn't present me as holy."],[1466.98,"They didn't represent God correctly."],[1469.62,"Part of Moses' job is to represent God to the people of Israel."],[1474.58,"How did he represent God?"],[1475.94,"He went out there and get got angry and yelled at them."],[1480.58,"God's like, did I call them disobedient?"],[1484.58,"Did I say any of that?"],[1487.3,"No. So that's the problem."],[1489.86,"Those are the two problems."],[1491.06,"Number one, I told you to do something and you didn't do it."],[1494.5,"You did something else."],[1496.5,"And number two, in doing that, you misrepresented me."],[1502.42,"Essentially lied about who God is."],[1505.06,"Misrepresented who God is. to the people"],[1508.3,"And Moses' main job, is representing God to the people and the people to God."],[1515.09,"So this is a major issue."],[1517.65,"And Aaron was right there with him."],[1520.21,"And so God is saying this to both Moses and Aaron, saying, because you did this, there's a consequence."],[1528.69,"You know, you're part of that generation that came out of Egypt, too."],[1533.41,"And was gonna make an exception for you."],[1537.54,"In theory, to go to go into the process line, but no exception now."],[1542.82,"So you're gonna leave them right up to it, and then in Moses' case."],[1548.42,"So again, God's not killing them."],[1550.02,"Moses is gonna live to be 120"],[1554.52,"Okay, instead of 120 in six months, because he led them across the Jordan River."],[1561.48,"And Aaron is still the high priest until the day he dies."],[1567.16,"His son will take over his high priest after him."],[1570.04,"God is not doing horrible things to them."],[1572.76,"But what did they just show?"],[1575.24,"They just acted like that generation that's dying in the wilderness."],[1583.37,"Fair's fair, is kind of what God's saying."],[1586.51,"If you're gonna behave like them, it wouldn't be right for me to give you special treatment that they didn't get."],[1592.59,"Verse 13 This was the water of contention, because the children of Israel scoffed before the Lord, and he was sanctified among them."],[1606.31,"They're talking about that, the spring of water there was called the water of contention because of the contention between the Israelites and God."],[1614.07,"Now we're going to see before we keep going."],[1617.59,"The book of Deuteronomy, when we get to the end of the book of Numbers, the Israelites are basically going to be ready to enter about to enter the land."],[1626.95,"So Deuteronomy is not like another leg of the journey or something."],[1631.35,"The book of what the book of Deuteronomy is, and of course we'll talk about this more when we get there, but what the book of Deuteronomy is, is. a final sermon that Moses gives to the people"],[1642.83,"Depterosnomos means second law or second Torah."],[1647.88,"Um, because in this sort of final sermon to the people, as they're about to go into the land and he's about to pass away, uh, Moses sort of reminds them of a lot of things."],[1661.12,"It reminds them of what they've experienced, reminds them of the command of command the commandments God has given."],[1668.3,"Reminds all these things."],[1669.42,"And so one of the things we're gonna see there, and we'll talk about this more in the book of Deuteronomy, the places where we see it, is that even this, Moses not being allowed to enter the land."],[1680.14,"You notice Moses. doesn't hue and cry and write all this"],[1685.3,"Um this kind of discipline, Moses is gonna receive and kind of learn from."],[1710.86,"We've been seeing that God has been working with Moses."],[1715.84,"And Moses has been being changed and transformed over this process."],[1720.16,"All these times where God has said, Look, I'm sick of these people."],[1725.12,"Why don't I just wipe them out and start over with you and your kids, Moses?"],[1728.89,"And Moses then goes and pleads with God, don't do that."],[1732.33,"As we've talked about, that's not because, oh, God was really mad and was really going to do that, but Moses was really smart and talked him out of it."],[1741.13,"But this was a process that he engaged in with Moses, where Moses is put in the position where these people who sometimes had just tried to murder him, he's asking God to bless them and to not punish them."],[1754.49,"Yeah, which didn't happen here."],[1756.25,"But we've seen that a lot in the past."],[1757.71,"And why why would God do that?"],[1759.55,"Why would God go through this?"],[1761.39,"Because it's been changing Moses."],[1764.01,"How he sees the people."],[1766.3,"And how he interacts with others. and how he understands who God is"],[1771.78,"Because, you know, we're gonna we're gonna see Christ, for example, ask his father to forgive the people who are murdering him while they're murdering him."],[1782.47,"So all of this, even stuff like this, is not, oh, God's really mad at Moses and is punishing him, and oh, he's taking this away from him."],[1792.16,"Even this is for Moses' benefit."],[1795.36,"And Moses is gonna see that."],[1797.76,"It's not only just theoretically, because of my view of God, oh, this must have benefited Moses somewhere."],[1803.04,"Moses is gonna tell us that."],[1804.96,"Uh in Deuteronomy."],[1807.92,"Now Moses sent messengers from Kadesh to the king of Edom saying, Thus says your brother Israel, you know all the hardship that befell us, how our fathers went down to Egypt, and we dwelt in Egypt a long time, and the Egyptians afflicted us and our fathers."],[1827.32,"But we cried out to the Lord, and the Lord heard our voice, and sent his angel and brought us up out of Egypt."],[1833.32,"Now here we are in Kadesh, a city just outside your borders."],[1838.12,"Okay. So if you know a little bit of the layout of the territories in the Levant at this point in history, so are folks generally familiar with the terms Cis Jordan and Transjordan?"],[1857.08,"Or is that just make you think about weird, weird cultural debates now"],[1863.28,"That's where the terms came from."],[1865.36,"So uh the Cis Jordan is the region between the Mediterranean Sea and the Jordan River."],[1873.84,"The Trans Jordan is the other side of the Jordan River."],[1878.96,"So you have the E basically the west side, I'll just say the west side of the Jordan River and the Dead Sea and the Sea of Galilee."],[1888.82,"The west side and then the east side."],[1891.62,"Now we're gonna have a rap feud or something, but um then the east side of the Jordan River and the Dead Sea and the Sea of Galilee."],[1899.0,"The east side is the Transjordan, the west side is the Cis Jordan."],[1901.16,"the So on the west side, coming up out of Sinai Peninsula, that's where the Philistines were."],[1902.08,"But I'll just say east side and west side."],[1912.8,"And Canaan is north of that."],[1915.52,"So if they went up on the west side of the Jordan River, they would have to go through Philistia to get to Canaan."],[1924.72,"So they're not going to do that."],[1926.56,"So the plan is Edom, the Edomites, are on the east side of the Dead Sea."],[1934.4,"And then Moab and Ammon are to the north of them, on the east side of the Jordan River."],[1940.56,"So the Edomites are descended from Esau from Edom, who's the brother, brother of Judah of Israel."],[1946.16,"So these are their cousins"],[1946.24,"So what Moses is doing here is he's sending messengers to the king of Edom to say, hey, remember us, your cousins."],[1957.96,"You know, we ended up being slaves in Egypt."],[1962.12,"God brought us out of Egypt."],[1963.8,"We're on our way to Canaan."],[1965.08,"We're just passing through."],[1966.84,"Can we pass through your territory on the way?"],[1971.26,"Because they're planning to go up on the east side of the Jordan River until they're past Philistia and then cross the Jordan River over into Canaan."],[1980.96,"That's their plan."],[1982.16,"But to do that, they have to go through Edom."],[1986.16,"Notice also, they remind us here in case you forgot."],[1989.2,"It says he. sent his angel and brought us up"],[1994.52,"Remember the angel of the Lord?"],[1996.28,"We talked about being Christ?"],[1999.64,"He's been with them this whole time."],[2002.2,"He didn't go away."],[2003.96,"He's gonna be with him through the rest of the Torah."],[2006.2,"He's gonna be with them through the whole book of Joshua."],[2008.36,"We're gonna see him a couple times in the book of Joshua."],[2011.32,"He's gonna end up leaving at the beginning of the book of Judges."],[2015.56,"So every once in a while we kind of forget because we don't see him coming out and talking to everybody every day."],[2022.57,"But that's the case."],[2024.87,"And notice here, so the actual Exodus, if we're gonna ask the question, who who bro brougughtht Israel out of Egypt?"],[2036.99,"There are actually three different answers that are given in different parts of the Old Testament."],[2041.63,"Those three answers are number one, obviously God."],[2045.25,"Yahweh. Number two, the angel of Yahweh, the angel of the Lord."],[2051.17,"Number three, the Spirit of God."],[2054.37,"Spirit of Yahweh brought them out."],[2057.01,"That's not coincidence."],[2058.53,"Okay? That's not something that Christians who believe in the Trinity like are reading back into the Old Testament."],[2065.73,"The Old Testament itself, in three different places, gives these three different answers."],[2070.37,"Here it says it was the angel of the Lord."],[2073.63,"So this is one of those places."],[2075.55,"There's a similar thing in the New Testament."],[2078.71,"In the New Testament, if you ask the question, who raised Jesus from the dead?"],[2083.75,"There are places that talk about God the Father raising him from the dead."],[2089.59,"There are places that just say Jesus rose from the dead, like he himself just writing like Christ says in St."],[2095.59,"John's Gospel, he could lay his life down and he could pick it up again."],[2099.53,"Meaning he's kind of raising himself."],[2102.09,"And 1 Corinthians 15 45 and other places, the Holy Spirit raised Christ from the dead."],[2108.65,"Again, that's not something that after the council of Nicaea we went and made up."],[2113.85,"It's the same three answers given to."],[2117.49,"A similar question."],[2118.45,"Because what do we celebrate at Posca at Passover now?"],[2122.73,"Christ's resurrection. The old Passover was the Exodus."],[2128.89,"So in both cases, if you ask the Bible who's responsible for Pasca, who's responsible for Passover, the answer you get is the Holy Trinity."],[2140.65,"So again, all this is just reading carefully."],[2144.17,"Trinity isn't something that gets made up later to try to explain things because things are confusing, or because they're like, hey, you know, the pagans have like thousands of gods, the Jews have like one God."],[2155.45,"Let's compromise on three."],[2157.23,"Like that's not one of four or one."],[2160.59,"That's not the that's not how any of this works."],[2163.25,"It's people reading carefully."],[2165.89,"But so at any r,ate this is the beginning of this very nice letter that Moses is sending to the king of Edom saying, Hey cousin, we just need a little need a little help from you."],[2176.81,"Verse 17 Let us pass through your country."],[2179.45,"We will not pass through fields or vineyards, nor will we drink water from wells."],[2183.77,"We will go along the king's highway."],[2185.93,"We will not turn aside to the right hand or the left until we pass through your borders."],[2189.95,"So he says, Look, we're not gonna."],[2192.35,"I know what you might be thinking."],[2194.19,"We're a big group of people."],[2196.37,"Big camp. We're gonna come, we're gonna start picking your fields clean of food."],[2201.74,"To feed ourselves."],[2203.26,"We're gonna drain your wells of water, you know, and you've got farmers, you've got, that are feeding your people."],[2210.16,"We're gonna keep going"],[2210.52,"We get that."],[2211.24,"We're not gonna do that."],[2212.2,"We're gonna stick on stay on the highway."],[2216.42,"Now they're not gonna drink from any of the wells in Edom."],[2219.46,"Where are they gonna get the water?"],[2221.78,"Which means it will follow them."],[2224.36,"So better say, we're not gonna touch anything."],[2226.36,"We're just gonna stay on the road."],[2227.72,"We're gonna pass right through."],[2229.16,"You won't even know we were here."],[2233.32,"Then Edom said to him, You shall not pass through me lest I come out against you in war."],[2239.48,"So that's not polite."],[2244.57,"They say, Nope, border is closed, my friend."],[2248.34,"Uh do not come."],[2250.02,"If you right, you pass through here, armies coming."],[2252.02,"here Now notice something."],[2252.18,"It says Edom said that"],[2257.26,"Now does that mean Esau, his ghost, came from beyond the grave and said that?"],[2263.02,"That's gonna be important later for some verses that we're gonna read."],[2267.1,"Like Jacob, I have loved, Esau, I have hated, and things."],[2270.52,"That often that name, even though it's the proper name of a person and the name of a whole country, it doesn't mean that person, it's referring to that historical person."],[2278.84,"It also doesn't mean like every person in that country, all said as one."],[2283.24,"No! Like, it's the king."],[2287.01,"So the children of Israel said to him, Now, again, this is not them all speaking in unison."],[2292.21,"This is Moses."],[2293.47,"We would go along the mountainous area."],[2295.39,"But if I or my cattle should drink any of your water, I would pay you"],[2300.63,"But the matter is nothing, let us pass along the mountainous area."],[2303.59,"So he's saying, Okay, we won't take the highway."],[2307.61,"The highway runs through nice land."],[2309.45,"You might not trust us, you might not believe us."],[2313.09,"But there's this mountainous area on the east end of Edom."],[2320.42,"We'll go through the mountains."],[2322.12,"So you don't have to worry, there's no fields there for us to pick."],[2325.4,"And hey, if it turns out we took anybody's water, we'll pay you for it."],[2329.64,"Whatever the going rate is, if you don't trust us."],[2333.08,"We promise. Let's let us go through that way."],[2337.24,"But he replied, You shall not pass through me."],[2339.84,"I should have stopped at you shall not pass."],[2341.68,"That would have been the You shall not pass through me."],[2344.72,"Now again, Moses and the people were not going to pass through the king."],[2350.0,"Like bad Mexican food."],[2351.84,"No. They were me is the country."],[2358.16,"The king is identified with right."],[2361.12,"The country itself."],[2363.6,"So Edom came out against him with a heavily armed multitude and with a strong hand."],[2367.76,"So they said troops out to the border."],[2371.94,"They're like, We don't trust you to not try something anyway."],[2375.48,"So we're so they send troops to the border."],[2380.2,"Thus, Edom refused to give Israel passage through his borders, and Israel turned away from him."],[2383.08,"Okay So this essentially makes it really inconveniences Israel because they have to go out further past Edom into the desert."],[2395.52,"And sort of go around the territory of Edom."],[2400.24,"And they're going to have to, once they get past Edom, they're going to have to either go through Moab or Ammon."],[2407.52,"They're going to have to try and talk to them, who are also kind of their cousins because they're descended from Abraham's nephew Lot."],[2413.45,"They're kind of related, kinfolk."],[2415.37,"They're going to have to find some way to go through there to get to the Jordan River and to cross it and to get to Canaan."],[2421.23,"Is the idea."],[2422.67,"So that's that's going to be the new plan."],[2424.83,"They're going to have to take this much longer, more cir.cuitous route"],[2432.87,"So the children of Israel, the whole congregation, journeyed from Kadesh and came to Mount Hoor."],[2439.03,"Then the Lord spoke to Moses and Aaron in Mount Hor by the borders of the land of Edom, saying, Let Aaron be added to his people, for ye shall not enter the land I am going I am giving to the children of Israel, because you provoked me at the water of controversy."],[2455.35,"Now, look, I try to be at least respectful to the people who translated the Orthodox Study Bible."],[2464.15,"But they couldn't translate this phrase the same way on the same page."],[2470.63,"Notice over in verse 13, it's the water of contention, and now here it's the water of controversy"],[2476.59,"People take Aaron and Eliezer his son and bring them up to Mount Horror before all the congregation."],[2484.11,"Strip Aaron of his robe and put it on Eliezer his son and let Aaron die there and be added to his people."],[2491.63,"So Moses did as the Lord ordered and took him up to Mount Whore before all the congregation."],[2495.79,"So let's pause there for a second."],[2497.07,"So Aaron gets told in advance, now's the time."],[2501.01,"You're gonna you're gonna pass away here at Mount Horror, you're gonna be buried here."],[2505.09,"They're kind of going along the border of Edom."],[2507.75,"To go around it."],[2509.19,"Um, and so the time has come for his eldest surviving son to become Eliezer, to become the new high priest."],[2516.47,"But notice the phrase that's used"],[2518.43,"So they're going to do this."],[2521.39,"We've pointed this out before, but it bears repeating."],[2524.51,"Because folks like Bart Urman think that Israelites and Jewish people did believe in an afterlife."],[2530.35,"But notice the phrase that's used when it talks about someone dying."],[2535.23,"Be added to his people."],[2537.55,"If they don't believe in an afterlife, that would be subtracted from his people."],[2541.89,"His people would be the people of Israel over there in the camp, and he's about to be subtracted, not added to them."],[2547.65,"He's being added to his people when he dies, that implies he's going to where his people, meaning his family, his ancestors, his fathers, are."],[2557.25,"He's going to rest with them in the place where they are."],[2560.17,"In the grave, Sheol."],[2560.61,"Yeah Seems kind of clear."],[2565.05,"But it's not to some people, apparently."],[2567.77,"Are they not his people?"],[2568.97,"What? Yeah. So Moses takes him to Mount Hor, as God told him."],[2574.81,"Then Moses stripped Aaron of his garments and put them on Eliezer, his son."],[2578.33,"And Aaron died there on top of the mountain."],[2580.97,"And afterward, Moses and Eliezer came down from the mountain."],[2584.49,"And all the congregation saw Aaron was dead, and all the house of Israel mourned for Aaron thirty days."],[2590.33,"Mariam's gone. Now Aaron's gone."],[2593.94,"So this is what I meant in We're transitioning."],[2597.22,"This is the next era."],[2599.54,"So Eleazar now is the second high priest."],[2604.34,"Yeah. And Aaron is buried there."],[2608.36,"Where they are."],[2613.32,"Listen next time as Father Stephen DeYoung continues his study of the scriptures on the Whole Counsel of God."],[2620.68,"Father Stephen's email address is wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."],[2626.04,"That's wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."]],"o":[{"t":23.52,"lv":2,"h":"Numbers 20 - Shift into the end game","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Left off where <b>genre shifts</b> again - Numbers covers ~<b>40 years</b> in the wilderness</li><li class=\"d1\">narrative episodes, commandments, liturgical instructions, <b>census</b> at start and end</li><li class=\"d1\">shifts can be abrupt but there's \"a rhyme and a reason\" - last time: who held the priesthood → commandments for priests</li><li class=\"d0\">Sinai to a few chapters into Numbers = <b>2 years</b>; rest of Numbers = <b>40 years</b> → spot-checking major events</li><li class=\"d0\">Pattern: event → material on its theme → next event</li><li class=\"d0\">Now: <b>pivot</b> - much closer to the end than the beginning</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Older generation dying off</b>, next generation coming of age, <b>preparing to enter Canaan</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"We've left the build up\"</li></ul>"},{"t":257.92,"lv":2,"h":"20:1 - Miriam dies at Kadesh","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Whole congregation in the desert of <b>Sin</b>, first month; people stay in <b>Kadesh</b>; <b>Miriam</b> dies and is buried</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Right off the bat\" - top three: <b>Moses</b> (leader), <b>Aaron</b> (high priest), <b>Miriam</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Miriam <b>led the song</b> after the Red Sea</li><li class=\"d0\">→ <b>beginning of the end</b> of that generation</li></ul>"},{"t":303.87,"lv":3,"h":"Desert of Sin and Kadesh","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Don't read into \"desert of <b>Sin</b>\" - not the English word; related to <b>Sinai</b> (the peninsula)</li><li class=\"d0\">Q: wasn't Kadesh north of Israel?</li><li class=\"d1\">depending on period, <b>far eastern edge of Egyptian power</b></li><li class=\"d1\">where Sinai Peninsula meets the <b>Levant</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Battle of Kadesh</b>: Egyptians vs <b>Hittites</b> who had come down the Levant</li><li class=\"d1\"><i>Exodus: Gods and Kings</i> (Christian Bale as Moses) - \"not a very good movie\" but first 20 min a great recreation of the battle; \"then turn it off\"</li></ul>"},{"t":398.0,"lv":3,"h":"Moving back toward Canaan","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Two things: <b>Miriam's death</b>, and they're moving <b>back closer to Canaan</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Not going straight up: God said back in Exodus - up the coast = <b>Philistine</b> territory</li><li class=\"d1\">five main cities: <b>Gath</b> (Goliath), <b>Ashkelon, Ashdod</b> - along the coast</li><li class=\"d1\">Philistines settled there after the <b>sea peoples</b> failed to invade Egypt</li><li class=\"d0\">God knew Israel would <b>chicken out</b> - too militarily powerful (they chickened out anyway)</li><li class=\"d0\">Teaser: more on Philistines and who they descend from in <b>Deuteronomy</b></li><li class=\"d0\">They'll <b>loop around</b> - the path comes in a few verses</li></ul>"},{"t":497.2,"lv":2,"h":"20:2-5 - No water; the people grumble","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">No water → gather <b>against Moses and Aaron</b>: \"would we had died with our brethren\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Why bring us into this desert to kill us <b>and our cattle</b>?\"</li><li class=\"d1\">sounds like their <b>parents</b>: \"why did you bring us here to die, Moses?\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>\"And our cattle\"</b> = Hebrew way of speaking to an extreme - \"what did the cow do?\"</li><li class=\"d1\">famous parallel: end of <b>Jonah</b> - \"don't you at least care about the cows?\"</li><li class=\"d0\">No <b>figs, vines, pomegranates</b>, no water</li><li class=\"d0\">Next generation <b>just as bad</b> - not obedient and wonderful</li><li class=\"d1\">God will stress in <b>Deuteronomy</b>: \"you didn't earn this\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"marginally better\" than the <b>Canaanites</b> with their real abominations</li></ul>"},{"t":626.05,"lv":2,"h":"20:6-8 - God's instruction: speak to the rock","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Moses and Aaron to the <b>door of the tabernacle</b>, fall on faces; <b>glory of the Lord</b> appears</li><li class=\"d0\">Lord: take the <b>rod</b>, gather the congregation, <b>speak to the rock</b> → it gives water for people and cattle</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Deja vu</b> - same water issue at the start in the wilderness (Exodus 17)</li></ul>"},{"t":659.71,"lv":3,"h":"The echo of Exodus 17: rod and rock","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Then: \"I'll stand on the <b>rock</b>, you <b>strike</b> it with the rod\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Rod = judgment</b> all through the Torah</li><li class=\"d1\">shepherd's rod for <b>discipline</b>; struck the <b>Nile</b> into blood → \"pronouncing judgment\"</li><li class=\"d0\">First case: dispute - Israel <b>accusing God</b>: \"you brought us out here to die\", imputing motives</li><li class=\"d0\">God standing on the rock = demonstration of the <b>humility of God</b></li></ul>"},{"t":752.08,"lv":3,"h":"The humble God and the humble Messiah","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Strange phrase\" - unique to the <b>God of Israel</b>: <b>humility</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Pharaoh</b>: God of a bunch of slaves can't be much - \"I'm head of the greatest superpower\"</li><li class=\"d0\">God identifies as God of <b>Abraham, Isaac, Jacob</b> - nomads with no country, living in tents</li><li class=\"d0\">Identifies with <b>orphans, widows, strangers, foreigners, the poor</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Points to <b>Jesus as Messiah</b> = anointed <b>king</b></li><li class=\"d1\">expect not a warrior, not <b>Herod's</b> or Caesar's son</li><li class=\"d1\">expect <b>peasants' son</b>, accused circumstances, born in a <b>cave</b>, laid in a <b>food trough</b>, \"dirt poor\"</li><li class=\"d0\">→ what you'd expect if the true God is <b>humble</b> and identifies with the humble</li></ul>"},{"t":922.37,"lv":3,"h":"The rock that followed them","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: 30-some years wandering - where's the <b>water</b> been coming from?</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Jewish tradition</b>: the original rock <b>followed them</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Midrash</b>: a <b>song</b> they sang to call the rock to catch up</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>St. Paul, 1 Cor</b>: \"Israel had a rock that followed them\" - no explanation - \"<b>the rock was Christ</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Paul receives Scripture <b>within a tradition of interpretation</b>, doesn't distinguish the two</li><li class=\"d1\">also <b>Jannes and Jambres</b> (to Timothy) = names of Pharaoh's court wizards - not in the Torah</li><li class=\"d1\">never says \"this isn't in the Bible, but...\"</li><li class=\"d0\">No bare text apart from a tradition of <b>reading, interpreting, copying, handing down</b> - \"you can't pry those apart\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1088.86,"lv":3,"h":"\"The rock\" - which one?","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">This time: <b>go to the rock</b> and <b>speak</b> to it</li><li class=\"d0\">Evidence in text for the following rock: God says <b>\"the rock\"</b> - not \"a rock\"</li><li class=\"d1\">not the only rock in Sinai; Moses \"immediately knew what rock it was\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Speak to it → God gives the Israelites water</li></ul>"},{"t":1150.66,"lv":2,"h":"20:9-11 - Moses strikes the rock twice","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Moses takes the <b>rod from before the Lord</b> - <b>Aaron's rod</b> that budded, kept in the most holy place</li><li class=\"d0\">Gathers congregation: \"<b>Hear me, you disobedient ones</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>Must we</b> bring water for you out of this rock?\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"danger, Will Robinson\" - Moses <b>and Aaron</b>? or Moses and God?</li><li class=\"d0\">Lifts hand, strikes the rock <b>twice</b> - water comes out abundantly</li><li class=\"d0\">Not supposed to hit it <b>twice</b>, nor present it as a <b>magic trick</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1224.44,"lv":3,"h":"What the strike meant","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">First strike = God <b>accepting the people's judgment</b> and giving <b>life</b> anyway</li><li class=\"d0\">Now Moses is <b>judging God</b> in front of the people</li><li class=\"d1\">angry at them, maybe a little at God - \"this again\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>taking credit</b> for the water</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Disobedient ones\" a nice translation of his anger</li></ul>"},{"t":1278.39,"lv":3,"h":"Leaders are more accountable","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Needed to understand the OT: looks minor - <b>lost his temper, whacked a rock</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Moses = <b>highest leadership position</b> possible for humans → <b>more accountable</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Q: what does a <b>monk on Mount Athos</b> confess?</li><li class=\"d1\">we live in the world - our sins would be \"number <b>378</b>\" on the list</li><li class=\"d1\">deal with the first 350 → 378 moves to the <b>top</b></li><li class=\"d1\">closer to God, what seems little is <b>big</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Moses talks to God <b>face to face</b> daily → \"this thing is huge\" - though low on my own list</li></ul>"},{"t":1413.26,"lv":2,"h":"20:12 - Judgment: no entry into the land","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Because you did not believe me to sanctify me before Israel, you shall <b>not bring this congregation into the land</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Odd translation: believe about what? - same word as <b>faith</b> in Greek</li><li class=\"d0\">Two charges:</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>not faithful</b> - didn't do what I told you</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>didn't sanctify</b> me - didn't present God as <b>holy</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Part of Moses' job = <b>represent God to the people</b>; instead got angry and yelled</li><li class=\"d1\">\"did I call them disobedient?\" → <b>misrepresented</b>, \"essentially lied about who God is\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Main job: <b>God to the people, people to God</b> → major issue; <b>Aaron</b> right there too</li></ul>"},{"t":1528.69,"lv":3,"h":"\"Fair's fair\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Consequence for both: part of the <b>Exodus generation</b>; an exception was possible, <b>no exception now</b></li><li class=\"d0\">God is <b>not killing them</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Moses lives to <b>120</b> - vs 120 in six months - just doesn't lead them across the <b>Jordan</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Aaron stays <b>high priest</b> until he dies; son takes over</li><li class=\"d0\">They just acted like the generation <b>dying in the wilderness</b></li><li class=\"d0\">If they behave like them - no special treatment they didn't get</li></ul>"},{"t":1592.59,"lv":2,"h":"20:13 - Water of contention; Moses' transformation","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Called the <b>water of contention</b> - Israel contended with God; he was <b>sanctified</b> among them</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Deuteronomy</b> = not another leg of the journey</li><li class=\"d1\">Moses' <b>final sermon</b> as they're about to enter; he's about to die</li><li class=\"d1\"><i>Deuteronomos</i> = <b>second law / second Torah</b></li><li class=\"d1\">reminds them of experiences and commandments</li><li class=\"d0\">There: Moses <b>doesn't hue and cry</b> about not entering - he learns from this discipline</li><li class=\"d0\">God has been <b>working with Moses</b>, changing him</li><li class=\"d1\">\"I'm sick of these people, wipe them out, start over with you\" → Moses <b>pleads for them</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not God really mad and Moses talked him out of it - a <b>process</b>: asking blessing for people who tried to murder him</li><li class=\"d0\">Changes how he sees <b>people, others, God</b></li><li class=\"d0\">→ Christ asks the Father to <b>forgive his murderers</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Even this is <b>for Moses' benefit</b> - Moses will say so in Deuteronomy</li></ul>"},{"t":1807.92,"lv":2,"h":"20:14-16 - Messengers to the king of Edom","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Moses sends from <b>Kadesh</b>: \"thus says your <b>brother Israel</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Recounts: fathers to Egypt, <b>afflicted</b>, cried out, Lord <b>sent his angel</b> and brought us out</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Here we are in Kadesh, just outside your borders\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1838.12,"lv":3,"h":"Geography: Cisjordan and Transjordan","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Cisjordan</b> = between the Mediterranean and the Jordan River; <b>Transjordan</b> = east side of Jordan, Dead Sea, Sea of Galilee</li><li class=\"d0\">West side from Sinai = <b>Philistia</b> - so they won't go that way</li><li class=\"d0\">Plan: east side - <b>Edom</b> east of the Dead Sea; <b>Moab and Ammon</b> north of them</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Edomites</b> descend from <b>Esau/Edom</b>, brother of Jacob/Israel → <b>cousins</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Ask: \"remember us, your cousins\" - just <b>passing through</b> on the way to Canaan</li><li class=\"d0\">Go up the east side past Philistia, cross the Jordan into Canaan</li></ul>"},{"t":1986.16,"lv":3,"h":"The angel of the Lord and the Trinity","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"He <b>sent his angel</b>\" - the <b>angel of the Lord</b> = Christ, with them all along</li><li class=\"d1\">through the Torah, <b>Joshua</b> (a couple of times), leaves at the start of <b>Judges</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Who brought Israel out of Egypt? <b>three answers</b> in the OT:</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Yahweh</b> / the <b>angel</b> of Yahweh / the <b>Spirit</b> of Yahweh</li><li class=\"d1\">not Trinitarians reading back - the <b>OT itself</b> says it</li><li class=\"d0\">NT parallel - who raised Jesus?</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>the Father</b> / <b>Jesus himself</b> (John: lay down and take up) / the <b>Holy Spirit</b> (1 Cor 15:45 and others)</li><li class=\"d1\">not made up after <b>Nicaea</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Pascha</b> = new Passover; old Passover = Exodus → who's responsible? the <b>Holy Trinity</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"Just reading carefully\" - not a compromise between pagan thousands and Jewish one: \"let's compromise on three\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2176.81,"lv":2,"h":"20:17-21 - Edom refuses passage","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Let us pass... not through <b>fields or vineyards</b>, nor drink from <b>wells</b>; the <b>king's highway</b>, no turning aside\"</li><li class=\"d1\">he knows the worry: big camp, <b>picking fields clean</b>, draining wells</li><li class=\"d1\">(water follows them anyway)</li><li class=\"d0\">Edom: \"You shall not pass through me lest I come out against you in <b>war</b>\" - \"border is closed, my friend\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Edom said\" - not Esau's ghost - name of person <b>and</b> country; it's <b>the king</b></li><li class=\"d1\">matters for later verses: \"Jacob I have loved, Esau I have hated\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Moses again: stay off the highway, go through the <b>mountainous area</b> - no fields</li><li class=\"d1\">if we drink any water, we'll <b>pay</b> - \"whatever the going rate\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Reply: \"You shall not pass through me\" - \"should have stopped at you shall not pass\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Me</b> = the country, identified with the king</li><li class=\"d0\">Edom sends a <b>heavily armed multitude</b> to the border - don't trust them</li></ul>"},{"t":2380.2,"lv":3,"h":"Israel turns away - the longer route","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Israel <b>turned away</b> - inconveniences them: out past Edom, around it through the desert</li><li class=\"d0\">Past Edom: try <b>Moab or Ammon</b> - kin, descended from Abraham's nephew <b>Lot</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Then Jordan, then Canaan - new, much <b>longer, circuitous route</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2432.87,"lv":2,"h":"20:22-29 - Aaron dies on Mount Hor","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Congregation journeys from Kadesh to <b>Mount Hor</b>, border of <b>Edom</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Lord: \"Let Aaron be <b>added to his people</b>... you provoked me at the <b>water of controversy</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">OSB couldn't translate the phrase the same way on the same page (<b>contention</b> v.13 / <b>controversy</b>)</li><li class=\"d0\">Take Aaron and <b>Eleazar</b>; strip Aaron's <b>robe</b>, put it on Eleazar; Aaron dies there</li><li class=\"d0\">Told in advance; buried at Hor; eldest surviving son becomes <b>new high priest</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>Added to his people</b>\" - <b>Bart Ehrman</b> and others say no afterlife belief</li><li class=\"d1\">if no afterlife it'd be <b>subtracted</b> from his people in the camp</li><li class=\"d1\">added = going to where his <b>family, ancestors, fathers</b> are - <b>Sheol</b>, the grave - \"seems kind of clear\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Moses and Eleazar come down; all Israel <b>mourned 30 days</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Miriam gone, Aaron gone → <b>next era</b>; Eleazar = <b>second high priest</b></li></ul>"}]});
